From: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 10:39:23 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: add 6.18 full-inline IPsec

Replace the legacy ECM inner-flow notifier with the Linux 6.18 Qualcomm PPE
provider API. Outbound SAs share a device-wide EIP tunnel and virtual port.
Each PPE flow retains its exact SA, XFRM state, and netdevice. Migrate
flows across rekey and recover encrypted SC8 exceptions through the host
route.
Keep transform-record lifetime counters synchronized.

Keep outer-inline receive and host lookaside as fallbacks. Match
the EIP-197 inner-flow ABI by converting network-order PPE L4 ports to
host-order values consumed by its hash builder. Quiesce provider callbacks
before module object teardown.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/169bf594df03ac4b29e0ccd3f6f87e70f0f3fb6e
Based-on: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/commit/39c0281b98922dcda04f91e30dd15bccbb0896ae
Signed-off-by: Himanshu Joshi <himajosh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Tushar Ganatra <tganatra@qti.qualcomm.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
